      "content": "In the housing projects, you'd see guys playing dominoes or cards, or just hanging out, smoking cigarettes and drinking from cans. The Puerto Rican guys might be playing music, like salsa or bomba, or just vibing to the sounds of Fania Records. The African American guys might be playing basketball or just chillin' on the stoop, shooting the breeze. You might also see some guys selling goods on the street, like knockoff jewelry or bootlegged records.\n\nNear the subway, you'd see guys loitering, looking for a score or a fight. They might be playing games like stickball or one-upmanship, or just trying to make a buck by selling newspapers or collecting cans. You might also see some guys just trying to stay warm, huddled up in their coats, waiting for the bus or a friend to show up.\n\nAs for specific \"street\" behaviors, you'd see guys using slang, like \"¿qué onda?\" or \"What's good?\", and using hand gestures, like the \" Bronx wave\" or the \" Puerto Rican salute\". You'd also see guys showing off their status, like wearing gold jewelry or displaying their tattoos. And, of course, you'd see guys",
